2 CONT '''Mu'izz ad-Din Malik Shah II''' (Turkish: Müizzeddin Melikşah, Persian: ملک شاه دوم‎) was Seljuq Sultan in Baghdad during 1105. He was the grandson of Malik Shah I, and was theoretically the head of the dynasty, although his rel
2 CONC ative Ahmed Sanjar in Khorasan probably held more effective power. He was deposed and killed by his uncle Muhammed Tapar.
