1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''NOTE:''' He may have died in 1169, not 1164. More research needed.
2 CONT
2 CONT * from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Toghrul III''' (Persian: طغرل‎; Modern Turkish: Tuğrul) (died 1194) was the last sultan of the Great Seljuq Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of sultan Arslan Shah, he succeeded him in 1175 or 1176. In 1190 he tried to free himself from the tutelage of the Atabeg of Azerbaijan, Kizil Arslan, but he was overthrown and imprisoned by the latter, who proclaimed hims
2 CONC elf sultan.[1] The usurper was assassinated the following year and Toghrul regained his throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 19 March 1194, he was defeated and killed near Ray[2] in the war that he had waged against the Shah of Khwarezm, Ala ad-Din Tekish. Toghrul's head was sent to the Caliph Al-Nasir who showed it in front of his palace in Baghdad.
2 CONC  The Great Seljuq Empire disappeared with Toghrul's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Grousset, Rene, The Empire of the Steppes, (Rutgers University Press, 1991), 158.
2 CONT * Grousset, 167.
