1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Suleiman II''', also known as Rukn ad-Din Suleiman Shah (Persian: رکن الدین سلیمان شاه‎), was the Seljuk Sultan of Rûm between 1196 and 1204.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Kilij Arslan II, he overthrew his brother, Sultan Kaykhusraw I, who had succeeded their father in 1192 and became sultan in 1196.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought neighbouring rulers and expanded the territories of the Sultanate. In 1201 he conquered Erzurum. Successful in the wars with the Byzantines, he was routed by the Georgians in the Battle of Basian of 1203.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by Kilij Arslan III in 1204–1205, after whom Kaykhusraw I ascended the throne for a second time.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Rum Sultanate of Rûm]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Charles Cawley (2006-07). "West Asia & North Africa, Chapter 2. Asia Minor. Seljukid Sultans of Rum". Foundation for Medieval Genealogy. Check date values in: |date= (help)
