1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hafize Hafsa Sultan''' [1] (Ottoman Turkish: حفصة سلطان, "the keeper one" and "young lioness"; c. 1492 or before - 10 July 1538) was an Ottoman princess, daughter of Selim I and, presumably, of his favorite Hafs
2 CONC a Hatun. She was therefore the sister or at least half-sister of Suleiman the Magnificent.[2] 
