1 TITL King of Imereti
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_VII_of_Imereti
2 CONT
2 CONT George VII was married four times. His first wife was Rodam, daughter of George XI of Kartli whom he married in 1703 and divorced in 1712. George then married his second wife, Tamar, a daughter of Giorgi-Malakia Abashidze, ex-wife
2 CONC  of Prince Giorgi Nizharadze, and repudiated the union in 1713 (she would marry her third husband Prince Merab Tsulukidze in 1714). He was then briefly married to Tamar, daughter of Papuna II, Duke of Racha, until her death in 171
2 CONC 4. In 1716, George married his fourth and last wife Tamar (Kochibrola; died 1742), daughter of Mamia III Gurieli.
2 CONT
2 CONT George VII was the father of four sons and four daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander V of Imereti (1703–1752), born of George's first marriage with Rodam of Kartli; King of Imereti (1720–1741, 1741–1746, 1749–1749).
2 CONT Mamuka of Imereti (died 1769), born by Rodam, King of Imereti (1746–1749).
2 CONT Princess Tamar (fl. 1735), born by Rodam, married to Prince David Abashide.
2 CONT Princess Tuta (fl. 1738), born by Rodam, married to Prince Papuna Chichua.
2 CONT Anonymous daughter (fl. 1735), born by Rodam, married to Mamuka, Prince of Mukhrani.
2 CONT George IX of Imereti (1718–1778), born of George's fourth marriage with Tamar Gurieli; King of Imereti (1741).
2 CONT Princess Ana (fl. 1726), born by Tamar Gurieli, married to Zaal, Eristavi of Guria.
2 CONT Prince Rostom (fl. 1746), born by Tamar Gurieli.
