2 CONT
2 CONT 2.3.3.2. Alexander Petrovich Trubetskoy (08/18/1792 - 04/14/1853), prince, participant in the Patriotic War of 1812 and foreign campaigns, colonel of the Semyonovsky Life Guards Regiment; in 1820, when it was disbanded, he was tra
2 CONC nsferred to the Kiev Dragoon Regiment. In 1826 retired colonel, landowner of the Kyiv district. He owned the estates of Gavronshchina in the Kyiv province and Inyutino in Nizhny Novgorod. He died in Nizhny Novgorod and was buried 
2 CONC in the Ascension Caves Monastery, next to his father.
2 CONT In 1816 A.P. Trubetskoy married Louise Valentinovna Rostsishevskaya (d. 1881).
2 CONT The marriage had four children:
2 CONT 2.3.3.2.1. Marya Alexandrovna Trubetskaya, married to Leonard Ludwigovich Madeisky, landowner, leader of the nobility of the Kyiv province (1854-1857).
2 CONT 2.3.3.2.2. Darya Aleksandrovna Trubetskaya (d. July 7, 1889), married a Pole Rylsky, and possibly became the grandmother of the Ukrainian poet Maxim Rylsky
2 CONT 2.3.3.2.3. Vladimir Alexandrovich Trubetskoy (1820, Kyiv - 1879), Voronezh governor, chairman of the Nizhny Novgorod chamber of the civil court. Wife - Maria Alekseevna Peshchurova (1817 - December 6, 1889). Vladimir Alexandrovich
2 CONC  was the native nephew of the prominent Decembrist Sergei Petrovich Trubetskoy and was brought up in his family ****.
2 CONT 2.3.3.2.4. Pyotr Alexandrovich Trubetskoy (1829 - 1893). the prince, a chamber junker, was with the Kiev-Volynsk and Podolsk governor-general. He died at the Gavronshchina estate, where he was buried. Wife - Elizabeth (? Ivanovna)
2 CONC  von Möller (1843 - 1886 ***). They had a son (? Vladimir). 
