1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_Loredan
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Francesco Loredan''' (Venice, 9 February 1685 – Venice, 19 May 1762) was a Venetian statesman of the Santo Stefano branch of the noble House of Loredan who served as the 116th Doge of Venice from the 18th of March 1752 until hi
2 CONC s death in 1762. Loredan was a man of modest culture and limited political experience, having been raised primarily for a life of commerce; in this he stood in stark contrast to his immediate predecessor, Pietro Grimani, who was a
2 CONC  poet and diplomat. Francesco Loredan was the only Doge to be awarded the Golden Rose.
2 CONT
