1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Şehzade Mahmud (1582/87 - 1602) was an Ottoman Prince, the eldest son of sultan Mehmed III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Şehzade Mahmud was born in Manisa in 1582/87, he was the eldest son of Mehmed III, who later ascended to the Ottoman Throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fearing the influence of his mother and his power and prestige, his death was due to Safiye Sultan's intringues. Sources Uzuncarsili, Ismail Hakki (1960). III Mehmed’in oglu sehzade Mahmud’un ölümü [The Death of Prince Mahmut, Son
2 CONC  of Mehmed III] (in Turkish). Belleten.
