1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gevherhan Sultan (ca. 1608 – 1660, Ottoman Turkish: گوھرخان سلطان‎, other names Güvherhan) was an Ottoman princess, the daughter of Ottoman Sultan Ahmed I (reign 1603-17) and his favourite consort Kösem Sultan. She
2 CONC  was the niece of Sultan Mustafa I (reign 1617-18 and 1622-23) and sister of Sultans Osman II (reign 1618-22), Murad IV (reign 1623-40), and Ibrahim (reign 1640-48).
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gevherhan_Sultan_(daughter_of_Ahmed_I)_  En]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Gevherhan Sultan was one of the four daughters of Ahmed I by Kösem Sultan (Other's being Ayşe Sultan, Fatma Sultan and Hanzade Sultan), who contracted multiple marriages that six times during their lifetime resulted in the promoti
2 CONC on of their spouses to the office of grand vizier. Gevherhan held the record among her siblings by her betrothal to three grand viziers: Öküz Mehmed Pasha, Topal Recep Pasha, and Siyavuș Pasha.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1619 she was married firstly to grand vizier Öküz Mehmed Pasha and became widow by his death. On her marriage to Mehmed Pasha the guests were entertained by Egyptian shadow players. Among these was the famous Davud el-attar (Me
2 CONC navi), whom Ahmed I had seen perform in Edirne, In 1624 she was married secondly to Topal Recep Pasha and again became widow by his death. After Receb's death she was betrothed to Siyavuș Pasha, but he died before the marriage cou
2 CONC ld take place. She had a son by her first husband and a daughter by her second husband.[citation needed] She died in 1660.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ottoman Empire
2 CONT     Ottoman dynasty
2 CONT     Ottoman family tree
2 CONT     Ottoman Emperors family tree (simplified)
2 CONT
2 CONT Further reading
2 CONT
2 CONT     Peirce, Leslie P., The Imperial Harem: Women and Sovereignty in the Ottoman Empire, Oxford University Press, 1993, ISBN 0-19-508677-5 (paperback).
2 CONT     Yavuz Bahadıroğlu, Resimli Osmanlı Tarihi, Nesil Yayınları (Ottoman History with Illustrations, Nesil Publications), 15th Ed., 2009, ISBN 978-975-269-299-2 (Hardcover).
